        <h2 class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-extrabold text-zinc-950 dark:text-white tracking-tight">
          4. The Neuroscience of Binaural Beats & Frequency Following Response (FFR)
        </h2>
        <p>
          First discovered by physicist Heinrich Wilhelm Dove in 1839, <strong>binaural beats</strong> are an auditory illusion produced in the brainstem's <em>Superior Olivary Complex</em>. When two pure sine wave tones with a slight frequency offset ($\Delta f$) are presented independently to each ear via stereo headphones, the brain integrates the phase differences and entrains electrical oscillations to match the difference frequency.
        </p>

